  "term": "intracranial hemorrhage",
  "definition": "Intracranial hemorrhage is bleeding inside the skull, a dangerous medical condition that can put pressure on the brain and cause severe complications or death. It includes several forms based on where the bleeding occurs, such as intraventricular, intraparenchymal, subarachnoid, epidural, and subdural hemorrhage.",
